s sued OpenAI, alleging copyright infringement. OpenAI and its backer Microsoft face similar copyright claims from prominent authors and news organizations, including the New York Times itself.",
   "Publishers are also contending with shrinking referral traffic as search engines roll out AI-generated answers that let users consume information without clicking through to websites. Google organic-search referrals to more than 2,500 websites fell 33% globally between November 2024 and November 2025, according to a Reuters Institute report citing data from Chartbeat."
  ],
