  "summary": "The New York Times, Agence France-Presse and The Economist on Monday joined more than 40 publishers in the Standards for Publisher Usage Rights (SPUR) coalition, which now counts more than 80 members across 20-plus countries. The member-funded coalition is building industry standards and technical systems \u2014 including a new Content Telemetry Standard \u2014 to track AI use of published content and enable licensing deals.",
