 {
  "author": "NewsVeria Newsroom",
  "body": [
   "Jim Harbaugh made clear Monday that the Los Angeles Chargers' roughest start in more than two decades has not fractured his relationship with team ownership. Speaking a day after a 23-17 home loss to the Denver Broncos dropped the Chargers to 0-5, Harbaugh said he and the Spanos family remain locked in on fixing it together.",
   "\"John Spanos, Dean Spanos, Susie Spanos, the whole Spanos family. It's shoulder to shoulder where we're in this fight together,\" Harbaugh said when asked whether he felt pressure from ownership to reverse course. He added that he is \"hell bent\" on turning things around.",
   "## Eight straight losses",
   "The defeat, played at SoFi Stadium, was the Chargers' eighth consecutive loss dating back to last season \u2014 the longest losing streak of Harbaugh's head-coaching career at the college or professional level, according to ESPN Research. It also marked the franchise's first 0-5 start since 2003.",
   "Harbaugh placed responsibility for Sunday's result squarely on himself, apologizing for a fourth-and-1 call against the Broncos that backfired. Quarterback Justin Herbert, who threw a league-high eight interceptions entering the game, turned the ball over twice and fumbled in the loss.",
   "## Injuries mount",
   "The Chargers' problems are compounded by a battered roster. Four rookies started on the offensive line, and Harbaugh listed a lengthening injury report: Joe Alt is undergoing testing for a neck issue, Kayode Awosika has a fibula injury, Ladd McConkey is emergency-only with a foot problem, and Tre' Harris is week-to-week with a hamstring injury.",
   "## Message to the locker room",
   "Harbaugh's message to his players was simple: \"Keep fighting. Keep being a leader. Keep being a competitor. Keep being the believer that you've been and even more.\"",
   "The road does not get easier. The Chargers travel to face the undefeated Kansas City Chiefs in Week 6 on Oct. 18, looking to avoid the franchise's first 0-6 start."
  ],
