 {
  "id": "art-0083-bills-rams-mnf-overtime-2026",
  "slug": "bills-rams-mnf-overtime-allen-first-ot-win-2026",
  "headline": "Bills Edge Rams 37-34 in Overtime Classic as Allen Finally Wins an OT Thriller",
  "socialHeadline": "Josh Allen's first career OT win: Bills 37, Rams 34 in a Monday night classic - Bass's 45-yarder seals it after a blocked kick",
  "summary": "Josh Allen threw for 210 yards and ran for 121 more as the Buffalo Bills beat the Los Angeles Rams 37-34 in overtime on Monday Night Football, with Tyler Bass kicking a 45-yard winner after Greg Rousseau blocked a potential Rams game-winner. Allen, 0-7 in overtime games entering the night, also reached his 100th career win.",
  "body": [
   "The Buffalo Bills outlasted the Los Angeles Rams 37-34 in overtime at SoFi Stadium on Monday night in one of the wildest games of the NFL season, with kicker Tyler Bass drilling a 45-yard field goal with 1:55 left in the extra period to end it.",
   "The winner came moments after defensive end Greg Rousseau blocked Rams kicker Harrison Mevis's potential game-winning 48-yard attempt, capping a chaotic finish. Mevis had also missed a 50-yarder earlier, and the Rams' kicking collapse defined the night.",
   "Josh Allen completed 12 of 19 passes for 210 yards with a touchdown and an interception, but did his heaviest damage on the ground: 121 rushing yards and a score. It was the first overtime victory of his career after seven previous OT defeats, and the 100th win of his career as a starter. \"That's the beautiful thing about football: You get another drive... Greg Rousseau made a play,\" Allen said, according to the Associated Press.",
   "Matthew Stafford was superb in defeat, going 40-of-54 for 383 yards and three touchdowns. Receiver Puka Nacua set a Monday Night Football record with 17 receptions for 138 yards and a touchdown.",
   "## Kicking collapse costs Rams",
   "Rams coach Sean McVay was blunt about special teams afterward. \"The kicking game, with our PAT, field goal (unit) - not even close to good enough... I'm going to evaluate everything,\" he said, per the AP. The Rams fell to 2-3 while Buffalo improved to 4-1.",
   "## Postgame scuffle",
   "The drama continued after the final whistle, when Rams left tackle Alaric Jackson struck Bills linebacker Bradley Chubb at midfield in an incident caught on ESPN's cameras. Chubb described it as an \"emotional game\"; the league had not announced any discipline as of Tuesday.",
   "## Fast start, frantic finish",
   "Buffalo opened the night with a 70-yard kickoff return from Ray Davis, and neither team led by more than one score after halftime. The win keeps the Bills (4-1) among the AFC's frontrunners, while the Rams (2-3) face a short week and serious questions about their kicking game."
  ],
  "category": "Sports",
  "tags": [
   "NFL",
   "Buffalo Bills",
   "Los Angeles Rams",
   "Josh Allen",
   "Monday Night Football"
  ],
  "publishedAt": "2026-10-13T07:45:00Z",
  "image": {
