 {
  "id": "art-0084-guardians-alcs-game1-rays-2026",
  "slug": "guardians-rally-alcs-game-1-rays-2026",
  "headline": "Guardians Rally Past Rays 7-3 to Take ALCS Game 1 on the Road",
  "socialHeadline": "Cleveland's kids come through: DeLauter's first postseason homer, Lowe's 2-run single breaks it open in the 8th - Guardians lead ALCS 1-0",
  "summary": "Rookie Chase DeLauter's first postseason home run and Nathaniel Lowe's tiebreaking two-run single in the eighth inning lifted the Cleveland Guardians to a 7-3 win over the Tampa Bay Rays in Game 1 of the ALCS on Monday night at Tropicana Field.",
  "body": [
   "The Cleveland Guardians struck first in the American League Championship Series, beating the Tampa Bay Rays 7-3 on Monday night at Tropicana Field to take a 1-0 series lead behind 14 hits and a late offensive surge.",
   "Tied 2-2 in the eighth, Nathaniel Lowe delivered the game's biggest hit - a two-run single that scored Jose Ramirez and Chase DeLauter and broke the game open. Ramirez added an RBI single in the ninth, his fourth straight postseason game with a run batted in, tying a franchise playoff record.",
   "## Rookie's night",
   "DeLauter, the rookie outfielder, went 3-for-4 with a solo homer in the sixth - his first career postseason home run - plus a double in the eighth. Patrick Bailey's tying homer in the seventh had briefly knotted the score at 2-2 before Cleveland pulled away.",
   "\"Cleveland is everything to me... This is the place I love, and they love me back,\" Ramirez said through an interpreter on the TNT broadcast.",
   "## Rays' streak ends",
   "The loss was Tampa Bay's first of the postseason. \"It's been a while since we've lost,\" Rays manager Kevin Cash said. Cleveland, meanwhile, won its fourth straight after rallying from 0-2 down against the White Sox in the ALDS. Game 2 is Tuesday night."
  ],
  "category": "Sports",
  "tags": [
   "MLB",
   "ALCS",
