 {
  "id": "art-0086-india-cjp-detained-jantar-mantar-2026",
  "slug": "india-cockroach-janta-party-leaders-detained-jantar-mantar-2026",
  "headline": "India Detains 'Cockroach' Party Leaders After Barricade Protest at Jantar Mantar",
  "socialHeadline": "Youth-led Cockroach Janta Party leaders detained in New Delhi after jumping barricades to 'reclaim' Jantar Mantar protest site",
  "summary": "Police in New Delhi detained leaders of the youth-led Cockroach Janta Party on Tuesday after they jumped barricades to enter Jantar Mantar, a day after the historic protest site was de-notified as an official demonstration venue. The group demands the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar over a voter-list revision it says removed over 130 million names.",
  "body": [
   "Indian police detained leaders of the youth-led Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) in New Delhi on Tuesday after they jumped barricades to \"reclaim\" Jantar Mantar, the capital's best-known protest site.",
   "Those detained included Ashutosh Ranka, Saurav Das and Ajinkya Shinde, along with around 20 volunteers, according to Reuters. The party's founder, Abhijeet Dipke, wrote on X: \"You cannot denotify the resistance.\" A CJP livestream showed volunteers jumping the gate and waving the Indian flag.",
   "## The demand",
   "The party - whose \"Cockroach\" name is its own chosen identity, not a slur - is demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar over a voter-list revision it claims stripped more than 130 million names. The Election Commission denies any wrongdoing.",
   "## Site de-notified",
   "Delhi Police announced Monday that Jantar Mantar would no longer be an official protest site, naming three alternative venues, according to police commissioner Anurag Kumar. The detentions came a day later."
  ],
  "category": "World",
