 {
  "id": "art-0087-us-opposes-china-coercion-2026",
  "slug": "us-state-department-opposes-china-coercion-belize-paraguay-2026",
  "headline": "US Says It Opposes Chinese 'Coercion' After Belize and Paraguay Ministers Sanctioned",
  "socialHeadline": "State Department backs Taiwan's diplomatic allies after Beijing sanctioned ministers of Belize and Paraguay over Taiwan ties",
  "summary": "The US State Department said Tuesday it opposes China's 'coercion and aggression' against countries in the Western Hemisphere, after Beijing sanctioned ministers from Belize and Paraguay - two of Taiwan's remaining diplomatic allies - over their ties with Taipei.",
  "body": [
   "The United States on Tuesday condemned what it called Chinese coercion of Latin American countries, after Beijing imposed sanctions on ministers from Belize and Paraguay over their governments' diplomatic ties with Taiwan.",
   "\"The Trump Administration opposes coercion and aggression by China against countries in our hemisphere for exercising their sovereign rights,\" State Department spokesperson Tommy Pigott said in a statement dated October 13, carried by Reuters. He cited Secretary of State Marco Rubio's position that the US \"will not allow our region to become a base of operation for adversaries, competitors, and rivals.\"",
   "\"We stand with our friends and partners, including Taiwan, to advance our shared prosperity, security, and values,\" Pigott added.",
   "## Taipei responds",
   "In Taipei, Taiwan's Deputy Foreign Minister Chen Ming-chi told parliament on Tuesday that Beijing's actions amounted to \"transnational repression.\"",
   "## Context",
   "China sanctioned the Belizean and Paraguayan ministers after both governments maintained diplomatic relations with Taiwan, which Beijing claims as its territory. The US statement marks a new development on top of the sanctions themselves."
  ],
  "category": "World",
  "tags": [
   "United States",
