 {
  "id": "art-0088-oregon-bear-alexander-iamaleava-2026",
  "slug": "oregon-bear-alexander-no-discipline-iamaleava-hit-2026",
  "headline": "Oregon's Dan Lanning Says Bear Alexander Won't Face Team Discipline for Hit on Iamaleava",
  "socialHeadline": "No team punishment for Oregon DT Bear Alexander over the play that injured UCLA QB Nico Iamaleava - but the Big Ten could still act",
  "summary": "Oregon coach Dan Lanning said Monday that defensive tackle Bear Alexander will not face team discipline for the second-quarter play that injured UCLA quarterback Nico Iamaleava in Saturday's 17-15 loss to the Bruins - though the Big Ten could still impose its own punishment.",
  "body": [
   "Oregon head coach Dan Lanning said Monday that defensive tackle Bear Alexander will not be disciplined by the team for the play that injured UCLA quarterback Nico Iamaleava during Saturday's 17-15 Bruins win at Autzen Stadium.",
   "In the second quarter, Alexander brought down Iamaleava, and replays appeared to show the lineman twisting the quarterback's helmet and swinging his right arm into his chin area. No flag was thrown on the play. Iamaleava suffered a knee injury and is expected to miss the rest of the season, with UCLA coach Bob Chesney describing \"serious concern.\"",
   "## Lanning's explanation",
   "\"Obviously [the punch is] late and it's not the way it needs to be done and wasn't executed the right way,\" Lanning said Monday, per ESPN. He added that Alexander told him, \"I wasn't trying to hurt the guy,\" and said the injury was to Iamaleava's lower extremity - not caused by the punch.",
   "## League review possible",
   "The Big Ten commissioner retains the authority to suspend Alexander, and the conference had not issued a statement as of Monday night, according to USA Today. The incident is distinct from the officiating controversy in the same game that the Big Ten already addressed."
  ],
