  "body": [
   "Florida State has dismissed its highest-rated 2026 signee. Freshman cornerback Chuck Kennon was removed from the Seminoles' roster on Monday, October 12, and a Florida State spokesperson confirmed Tuesday morning that the dismissal was for \"conduct detrimental to the team.\"",
   "Kennon was the jewel of FSU's 2026 class: ranked No. 51 overall and the No. 6 cornerback nationally by 247Sports with a grade of 97, he was one of just three Top247 signees for the Seminoles. The Sarasota, Florida native committed to Florida State on July 6, 2025, choosing the Seminoles over more than 36 offers including Georgia, Florida and Miami.",
   "He enrolled at FSU in early January 2026 but barely saw the field, appearing in just one game this season \u2014 for a single snap late in the October 3 win over Virginia.",
   "## Second removal in a week",
   "Kennon is the second Florida State player removed in a week, following running back Gemari Sands' removal the prior week. No specific details of misconduct have been made public, and no legal accusation has been reported \u2014 the program has framed it strictly as a team disciplinary matter.",
   "The dismissal comes at a difficult moment for the Seminoles, who sit at 3-3 (1-2 in the ACC) and travel to face unbeaten Miami on Saturday, October 17 at 7 p.m. ET on ESPN."
  ],
