 {
  "body": [
   "The Jacksonville Jaguars will be without their starting left tackle for a stretch. Anton Harrison is expected to have arthroscopic surgery on his right knee after the team returns from London and will miss multiple games, according to ESPN's reporting from Ian Rapoport and Jeremy Fowler on October 13, 2026.",
   "The injury happened early in the third quarter of Sunday's 19-17 win over the Philadelphia Eagles at Tottenham Hotspur Stadium. Harrison spun on the field turf to make a block and twisted his knee planting his right leg; he was carted to the locker room and underwent testing on Monday.",
   "## Timeline uncertain",
   "The recovery window won't be known until the procedure: reports put it at three to five weeks, which would mean an injured-reserve stint, or three to four months \u2014 potentially season-ending \u2014 depending on what surgeons find.",
   "Harrison will not play in Sunday's game against the Houston Texans (1-4) at Wembley Stadium. Backup Walker Little, with 39 career starts over six seasons, is expected to step into the lineup. Coach Liam Coen described the injury as \"a weird play,\" saying Harrison was blocking on a turnback when the knee tweaked.",
   "## A big loss up front",
   "Harrison, 24, was Jacksonville's 27th-overall pick in the 2023 draft out of Oklahoma, has started 53 games, and moved from right tackle to left tackle this season for the 4-1 Jaguars. The same London game also cost the Jaguars long snapper Ross Matiscik to a right shoulder injury, with veteran Jacob Bobenmoyer signed as his replacement."
  ],
