 {
  "body": [
   "One man died and four other people were injured Monday afternoon in an incident at Six Flags Over Georgia, in Cobb County near Atlanta. The incident happened at about 3:58 p.m. local time on October 12, 2026, and the park closed for the remainder of the day.",
   "## Investigation underway",
   "The Cobb County Police Department's Major Crimes Unit is investigating. The county's Department of Emergency Communications confirmed the death; the victim's identity has not been released and the official cause has not been determined.",
   "Witnesses told Atlanta television stations they saw a man fall from the Goliath roller coaster, with at least two saying he struck parts of the ride before hitting the ground. That account of how the fall happened comes from witnesses and has not been confirmed by authorities \u2014 the official circumstances remain under investigation.",
   "The park issued a statement offering condolences, saying it is supporting affected guests and staff and cooperating with investigators, and declined further detail out of respect for the family's privacy. Riders were evacuated from the stopped train via emergency stairs.",
   "## Similar rides closed as a precaution",
   "Six Flags closed similar Bolliger & Mabillard coasters \"out of an abundance of caution\" while the incident is examined \u2014 nine rides at parks across North America, including Raging Bull at Six Flags Great America, Goliath at Six Flags Magic Mountain, Nitro at Six Flags Great Adventure, Leviathan and Behemoth at Canada's Wonderland, Fury 325 and Thunder Striker at Carowinds, and Orion and Diamondback at Kings Island.",
   "Goliath opened in 2006: a roughly 200-foot hyper coaster built by Switzerland's Bolliger & Mabillard, with a top speed near 70 mph and a clamshell lap-bar restraint."
  ],
  "breaking": false,
  "category": "US",
