  "id": "art-0096-france-saudi-airport-advisory-2026",
  "slug": "france-warns-citizens-avoid-saudi-airports-houthi-strikes",
  "headline": "France Tells Citizens to Avoid Saudi Airports as Houthi Strikes Continue",
  "socialHeadline": "France formally advises its citizens: don't use Riyadh, Jeddah or Dammam airports \u2014 exit via Doha or Manama",
  "summary": "France's foreign ministry is formally advising its nationals not to use or transit the airports of Riyadh, Jeddah and Dammam and to avoid travel to those cities except for imperative reasons, citing deadly Houthi strikes in recent days.",
  "category": "world",
  "tags": [
   "France",
   "Saudi Arabia",
   "Travel Advisory",
   "Houthis",
   "Aviation"
  ],
  "publishedAt": "2026-10-13T21:04:09Z",
  "status": "PUBLISHED",
  "breaking": false,
  "editorPick": false,
  "pinned": false,
  "image": {
   "src": "/images/media-generation-nv-france-saudi-travel-advisor-0-f13f11a7-ec3e-4508-a101-70160bb441e2.webp",
   "alt": "Flat infographic illustration of an airplane over a stylized map with a warning sign and location pin near an airport control tower",
   "caption": "Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.",
   "credit": "NewsVeria generated illustration"
  },
  "body": [
   "France's foreign ministry is formally advising its nationals not to use or transit the airports of Riyadh, Jeddah and Dammam, and to avoid travel to those three cities except for imperative reasons, citing deadly Houthi strikes in recent days.",
   "## What the advisory says",
   "The guidance, published in France Diplomatie's 'last-minute alerts' section for Saudi Arabia, recommends that French citizens wishing to leave the country travel via Doha in Qatar or Manama in Bahrain instead. The southern border areas of Najran, Abha, Khamis Mushait and Jazan remain formally discouraged for travel.",
   "## The strikes behind it",
   "The advisory cites Houthi strikes described as deadly against Riyadh's airport and the city of Dammam in recent days. France confirmed on October 11 that a French woman was injured in the October 10 attack. No newer strikes had been reported as of October 13, and Britain has issued parallel guidance to its own citizens.",
   "## No casualty figures",
   "NewsVeria is not publishing casualty tolls from these attacks: figures circulating in different outlets conflict sharply, and no single verified official count is available."
  ],
  "sources": [
   {
    "name": "France Diplomatie \u2014 Saudi Arabia: last-minute alerts (official travel advisory)",
    "role": "primary",
    "url": "http://www.diplomatie.gouv.fr/fr/information-par-pays/arabie-saoudite/dernieres-minutes-et-alertes"
   },
