  "headline": "WNBA Moves Finals Games 3 and 4 to State Farm Arena in Atlanta",
  "socialHeadline": "WNBA Finals head to State Farm Arena: Games 3 and 4 move to a 17,000-seat stage",
  "summary": "The WNBA announced on October 13, 2026 that Games 3 and 4 of the Finals between the Atlanta Dream and Golden State Valkyries will be played at State Farm Arena, expanding capacity from 3,500 to 17,044 seats.",
  "category": "sports",
  "tags": [
   "WNBA",
   "Atlanta Dream",
   "Golden State Valkyries",
   "WNBA Finals",
   "State Farm Arena"
  ],
  "publishedAt": "2026-10-13T21:06:05Z",
  "status": "PUBLISHED",
  "breaking": false,
  "editorPick": false,
  "pinned": false,
  "image": {
   "src": "/images/media-generation-nv-wnba-finals-arena-illustrat-0-c3485337-aadb-45ee-80bd-c36497f57442.webp",
   "alt": "Flat infographic illustration of a basketball arena bowl with a championship trophy and basketball",
   "caption": "Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.",
   "credit": "NewsVeria generated illustration"
  },
  "body": [
   "Games 3 and 4 of the 2026 WNBA Finals will be played at State Farm Arena in Atlanta, the league announced Tuesday, giving the Atlanta Dream a far bigger stage for the franchise's first Finals games since 2013.",
   "## New dates and bigger building",
   "Game 3 has been moved a day earlier to Wednesday, October 21 at 8 p.m. ET. Game 4 remains on October 24 but tips off at 1 p.m. ET instead of 3:30 p.m., a shift made to accommodate the Atlanta Hawks' home opener against the Houston Rockets that evening. The move expands capacity from the Dream's 3,500-seat Gateway Center Arena to 17,044 seats.",
   "## Why the switch",
   "The league said the change resolves scheduling conflicts at the Dream's usual home while putting the championship round in a major arena. Commissioner Cathy Engelbert credited the Dream, the Valkyries, the Hawks, arena staff and the league's NBC/Universal broadcast partners with making the move possible. Tickets go on sale Friday at 10 a.m. ET.",
   "The best-of-seven series pits the Dream against the expansion Golden State Valkyries. One scheduling wrinkle remains unresolved: a potential Game 6 on October 29 still conflicts with a Hawks-Cavaliers game."
  ],
  "sources": [
   {
    "name": "Reuters \u2014 WNBA Finals Games 3 and 4 moved to State Farm Arena",
